  "authoringNote": "D2 regression (checkpoint #22): one finding keeps every held condition with its own routing. R03 checks each current usable order separately (C09): A is complete; B states no signature metadata, so R03.element_missing (element.signature, B) holds, missing, authorization coordinator, needs_information. The orders state different non-null dates and quantities, so R03.orders_disagree holds twice, once per field (order.date and order.quantity), each naming A and B. Signature is not a disagreement because B states null (a value beside null). R03 status is conflict (first outcome owning a held condition), administrative reviewer, and the missing condition stays beneath it. R04 reads both final encounters and orders: the encounters disagree (encounters_disagree, encounter.date, E1 and E2); the orders disagree (orders_disagree, order.date, A and B); pair (E2 2026-09-03, A 2026-09-01) is order_before_encounter; pair (E2, B) is the same date without times, so same_day_unsequenced (manual_review beneath conflict, C02); pairs (E1, A) and (E1, B) are sequenced within the bound with equal identifiers. R04 is conflict. R05: each receipt references its order version and follows the order span end (2026-09-02T12:00Z for A, 2026-09-04T12:00Z for B), so R05 passes. Parent sets are empty (no restricted, unreadable or failed-provenance condition). Citations: R01 seven supplier fields and both codes (nine); R02 twelve; R03 nine for A and seven for B (no signature facts); R04 twelve; R05 three per receipt and both order dates (eight); R06 ten; R07 two. State needs_human_review.",
